{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory safely moved from initial red-flag screening and medication uncertainty to same-night ED evaluation/observation, then to written discharge-medication reconciliation, red-flag return precautions, and short-term refill planning. No serious or minor responsibility-chain failure is present: the doctor repeatedly avoided anchoring on neuralgia, prevented self-adjustment of antithrombotic/cardiovascular drugs, tracked pending CT/coagulation/biochemistry results, and obtained an executable family plan. High-order credit is valid for correcting family/patient misunderstandings and dynamically reprioritizing from home medication questions to ED/observation and later continuity/refill planning, but the trajectory is not Perfect because hidden vascular-record discovery was not fully completed and occipital neuralgia-vs-vascular verification did not cover all required pain-feature details.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00659",
        "explanation": "The final doctor plan confirms ongoing medication timing, urgent return precautions, and refill pathway.",
        "quote": "利伐沙班绝不能断"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00659",
        "explanation": "The final doctor plan provides clear night-time emergency triggers.",
        "quote": "立即去急诊，不要等"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode closes after hospital evaluation, written discharge instructions, home medication separation, red-flag understanding, and a concrete refill/follow-up pathway. Remaining risks are bounded: headache etiology is not definitively solved, but urgent triggers, medication safety, and continuity actions are clear.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
